# Expectation record for 04_bitfields/003_compound_assignment.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_compound_assignment
area               = 04_bitfields
description        = Compound assignment operators +=, -=, |=, &=, ^=, <<= and >>= applied to bitfields, folded and volatile runtime variants
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
The default undefined-behaviour warning gate applies unmodified, with no deviation:
-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror.  The program
was verified to pass that gate and to run cleanly under
-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all.

Every right-hand constant lies inside its destination field's representable range, and every
intermediate result stays inside the field, so no conversion can change a value and no signed
overflow can occur.  The unsigned decrements use an unsuffixed literal, keeping the
subtraction in int arithmetic rather than unsigned arithmetic that could wrap.

Shift safety is enforced by construction.  No left shift is ever applied to a negative value,
which would be undefined: the unsigned field holds 27 before its left shift and the signed
field holds 21, and both results (54 and 42) remain inside their fields.  No right shift is
ever applied to a negative value either, so the implementation-defined choice of arithmetic
versus logical right shift is not relied upon anywhere in this program.  Every shift count is
strictly less than the width of the promoted operand.

Bitwise or, and and exclusive-or are applied only while the signed field holds a non-negative
value, so no dependence on the representation of a negative signed value arises.  Negative
signed values are exercised only through addition and subtraction.

No aliasing violation: no pointer is formed to any bitfield and no type-punning occurs.  No
uninitialized read: both objects have explicit constant initializers, and the volatile object
additionally has static storage duration.  No object is modified twice between sequence points;
each compound assignment is a separate full statement, and each print is a separate statement
after it.  No pointer value, address, timestamp, random value or locale-dependent format is
printed.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Every bitfield is declared with an explicit signed int or unsigned int base type.  A plain
int bitfield's signedness is implementation-defined, so using it would manufacture a spurious
divergence; stating the signedness in the declaration removes that dependency entirely.  All
seven compound operators are applied to an unsigned field and to a signed field, so both
signednesses are exercised by every operator the requirement names.

Plain char is not used.  Plain char signedness was measured to differ across the four targets
(signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64), so it is avoided entirely.

No value whose width varies by target is printed.  sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) differ on
i686 (4) from the other three targets (8), so neither is printed, and no pointer value or
address appears in the output.  Every bitfield is declared on an int base type, and int is
four bytes on all four targets, so every printed value is target-invariant by derivation.
Every printf argument is explicitly cast to unsigned or int.

The folded and runtime halves of the output are deliberately value-identical: the first is the
constant folder's answer and the second is computed at run time through volatile storage, which
forces real load, extract, operate, insert and store sequences.  Their equality is itself an
assertion, and it is what makes this program able to distinguish a constant-folding defect from
a code-generation defect.

All four targets and all three oracles remain enabled.  Bitfield layout, read-back values and
the minimum value of a narrow signed field were measured identical on all four targets, so a
cross-backend divergence here is a genuine finding rather than an implementation-defined
difference.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
folded_u6_add=8
folded_u6_sub=7
folded_u6_or=31
folded_u6_and=30
folded_u6_xor=27
folded_u6_shl=54
folded_u6_shr=13
folded_s7_add=8
folded_s7_sub=6
folded_s7_or=23
